{
  "an5.139:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.139 ",
  "an5.139:0.2": "14. Kings ",
  "an5.139:0.3": "Cannot Endure ",
  "an5.139:1.1": "“Mendicants, a royal bull elephant with five factors is not worthy of a king, not fit to serve a king, and is not reckoned a factor of kingship. ",
  "an5.139:1.2": "What five? ",
  "an5.139:1.3": "It’s when a royal bull elephant can’t endure sights, sounds, smells, tastes, and touches. ",
  "an5.139:2.1": "And how is it that a royal bull elephant can’t endure sights? ",
  "an5.139:2.2": "It’s when a royal bull elephant gone to battle falters and founders at the sight of a division of elephants, of cavalry, of chariots, or of infantry. It doesn’t stay firm, and fails to plunge into battle. ",
  "an5.139:2.3": "That’s how a royal bull elephant can’t endure sights. ",
  "an5.139:3.1": "And how is it that a royal bull elephant can’t endure sounds? ",
  "an5.139:3.2": "It’s when a royal bull elephant gone to battle falters and founders at the sound of a division of elephants, of cavalry, of chariots, or of infantry, or the thunder of the drums, kettledrums, horns, and cymbals. It doesn’t stay firm, and fails to plunge into battle. ",
  "an5.139:3.3": "That’s how a royal bull elephant can’t endure sounds. ",
  "an5.139:4.1": "And how is it that a royal bull elephant can’t endure smells? ",
  "an5.139:4.2": "It’s when a royal bull elephant gone to battle falters and founders when it smells the odor of the feces and urine of battle-hardened, pedigree royal b